">0.93046</td></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="left" valign="top">Clearance below 60 ml/min</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">5 (7.9)</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">10 (15.9)</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">1 (5)</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">3 (13)</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top"/></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="left" valign="top">Total cholesterol (mg/dl)</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">209.27 &#x000b1; 45.63</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">206.90 &#x000b1; 46.05</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">244.30 &#x000b1; 57.65</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">224.54 &#x000b1; 48.62</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">0.01976</td></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="left" valign="top">Triglycerides (mg/dl)</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">165.78 &#x000b1; 78.42</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">182.48 &#x000b1; 132.40</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">170.95 &#x000b1; 115.87</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">151.42 &#x000b1; 46.02</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">0.90922</td></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="left" valign="top">Fibrinogen (mg/dl)</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">407.43 &#x000b1; 116.5</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">442.67 &#x000b1; 114.57</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">379.7 &#x000b1; 113.56</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">351.46 &#x000b1; 63.15</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">0.00007</td></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="left" valign="top">Interleukin-6</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">15.96 &#x000b1; 8.84</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">14.21 &#x000b1; 14.21</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">ND</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">ND</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top"/></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="left" valign="top">hsCRP</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">10.75 &#x000b1; 23.08</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">12.37 &#x000b1; 23.79</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">7.44 &#x000b1; 15.54</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">3.84 &#x000b1; 4.39</td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="top">0.00763</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>Data are means &#x000b1; SD or <italic>n</italic> (&#x00025;) of patients.</p></fn><fn id="t1fn1"><label>&#x0002a;</label><p>Diabetes was defined according to World Health Organization/American Diabetes Association criteria; in all probands without known history of diabetes, diabetes was ruled out by an oral glucose tolerance test.</p></fn><fn id="t1fn2"><label>&#x02020;</label><p>Hypertension defined by the use of antihypertensive drugs and/or systolic blood pressure &#x0003e;140 and/or diastolic blood pressure &#x0003e;90 mmHg.</p></fn><fn id="t1fn3"><label>&#x02021;</label><p>Dyslipidemia defined by use of lipoid lowering drugs and/or HDL &#x0003c;35 mg/dl, triglycerides &#x0003e;170 mg/dl, and total cholesterol &#x0003e;240 mg/dl. CAD, angiographically proven coronary artery disease; MI, myocardial infarction; ND, not done; OAD, oral antidiabetic drug.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>